      "content": "Propranolol is a beta-blocker that can actually be dangerous for people with asthma because it blocks the receptors needed to keep your airways open, potentially triggering a severe attack. Since you have asthma, you should absolutely not take this medication without a direct prescription and supervision from a doctor who knows your specific lung history. Instead, try taking deep breaths or drinking some water to calm your nerves before your presentation.",
